The tramaj specification: language reference, wire format, and the shipped v3/v4 extensions.

=base:main-content.cmark

# Reference

These pages are generated straight from the specs in the
[tramaj repository](https://github.com/lucasdicioccio/tramaj/tree/main/specs)
— the repository is always the canonical source, and may be ahead of what's
published here.

- [**Language reference**](/reference-language.html) — core AST, values,
  evaluation rules, surface syntax and its desugarings, imports, actions,
  builtins, and what's implementation-defined. Start here.
- [**Node JSON representation**](/reference-node-json.html) — the normative
  wire format for the evaluated `Node` AST.
- [**v3 — Symbolic values and constraints**](/reference-v3-symbols.html) —
  `?(key)` allocation, `!constraint(name, ...)`, and the `Symbolic`
  evaluation mode.
- [**v4 — Types**](/reference-v4-types.html) — the nominal type algebra,
  type parameters through imports, and typed annotations.

Two more documents exist only in the repository, not mirrored here since
they're development history rather than language reference:

- [`laws.md`](https://github.com/lucasdicioccio/tramaj/blob/main/specs/laws.md)
  — the design invariants, rewritten in prose on the
  [Properties](/properties.html) page.
- [`decisions.md`](https://github.com/lucasdicioccio/tramaj/blob/main/specs/decisions.md)
  — the resolved-conflicts log: which reading won wherever the design drafts
  disagreed, and why.

Earlier, superseded design drafts live under
[`specs/archive/`](https://github.com/lucasdicioccio/tramaj/tree/main/specs/archive),
kept for the reasoning in them rather than as current documentation.

